Gears of War 3: speckled post-processing (depth of field) at 2x / 3x internal resolution. Gears 3
draws its scene into a 1x render target and resolves the same EDRAM as a 4x MSAA surface of half
the size, for a free 2x2 downsample that the depth of field passes blur and blend back. With
resolution scaling, the ROV pixel shaders and the resolve shaders placed each MSAA sample by the
host pixel index ((host_pixel << sample_count_log2) + sample bits), so the sample bit and the host
subpixel bit traded places and the 1x and 4x views stopped lining up: the downsample averaged the
wrong pixels (fine purple speckle in shadowed areas). The samples are now arranged per guest pixel
with the host subpixel carried along (((host_pixel / scale) << sample_count_log2 + sample bits) *
scale + host_pixel % scale), the scaling part of Xenia 437a7280cf, keeping this layout's sample order:
- dxbc_translator_om.cpp: the ROV sample 0 position, and the steps to the other samples (scale rows /
  scale columns instead of 1);
- ResolveEdramInfo.guest_samples (bit 30): set for ROV resolves with scaling, read by the scaled
  resolve shaders, which are replaced from sdk/shaders/d3d12_5_1 (see sdk/shaders/README.md).
No change at 1x, on the RTV path or on Vulkan. gpu_edram_scaled_guest_samples (default true, restart)
turns it off.

